Feature: Audit Log # specs/features/audit_logs.feature:1
  As an administrator
  I want to view audit logs of all changes
  So that I can track who changed what and when
  Background:   # specs/features/audit_logs.feature:6

  @admin
  Scenario: View audit logs                              # specs/features/audit_logs.feature:11
    Given the API is running                             # specs/steps/company_steps.py:10
    And I am logged in                                   # specs/steps/system_steps.py:52
    When I retrieve the audit logs                       # specs/steps/audit_steps.py:11
    Then I see a list of audit log entries               # specs/steps/audit_steps.py:22
    And each entry shows: table_name, action, changed_at # specs/steps/audit_steps.py:29

  @admin
  Scenario: Filter audit logs by table                 # specs/features/audit_logs.feature:17
    Given the API is running                           # specs/steps/company_steps.py:10
    And I am logged in                                 # specs/steps/system_steps.py:52
    Given audit logs exist for multiple tables         # specs/steps/audit_steps.py:37
    When I filter audit logs by table "companies"      # specs/steps/audit_steps.py:43
    Then I see only audit logs for the companies table # specs/steps/audit_steps.py:55

  @admin
  Scenario: Filter audit logs by action           # specs/features/audit_logs.feature:23
    Given the API is running                      # specs/steps/company_steps.py:10
    And I am logged in                            # specs/steps/system_steps.py:52
    When I filter audit logs by action "INSERT"   # specs/steps/audit_steps.py:63
    Then I see only audit logs with INSERT action # specs/steps/audit_steps.py:74

  @admin
  Scenario: View audit log details       # specs/features/audit_logs.feature:28
    Given the API is running             # specs/steps/company_steps.py:10
    And I am logged in                   # specs/steps/system_steps.py:52
    Given an audit log entry exists      # specs/steps/audit_steps.py:82
    When I retrieve the audit log detail # specs/steps/audit_steps.py:92
    Then I see the old and new values    # specs/steps/audit_steps.py:106

  @viewer
  Scenario: Viewer cannot access audit logs  # specs/features/audit_logs.feature:34
    Given the API is running                 # specs/steps/company_steps.py:10
    And I am logged in                       # specs/steps/system_steps.py:52
    Given I am logged in as "viewer"         # specs/steps/system_steps.py:58
    When I try to retrieve audit logs        # specs/steps/audit_steps.py:119
    Then the audit operation is denied       # specs/steps/audit_steps.py:113

Feature: User Authentication # specs/features/authentication.feature:1
  As a registered user
  I want to authenticate securely
  So that I can access the system according to my role
  Background:   # specs/features/authentication.feature:6

  Scenario: User logs in successfully               # specs/features/authentication.feature:14
    Given the Supabase authentication is configured # specs/steps/system_steps.py:37
    And the following users exist                   # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:10
      | email               | role    | full_name    |
      | admin@empresa.com   | admin   | Admin User   |
      | analyst@empresa.com | analyst | Analyst User |
      | viewer@empresa.com  | viewer  | Viewer User  |
    Given I am on the login page                    # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:92
    When I enter valid credentials                  # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:186
    Then I am redirected to the dashboard           # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:192
    And my role is displayed in the header          # None

  Scenario: User logs in with invalid credentials           # specs/features/authentication.feature:20
    Given the Supabase authentication is configured         # specs/steps/system_steps.py:37
    And the following users exist                           # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:10
      | email               | role    | full_name    |
      | admin@empresa.com   | admin   | Admin User   |
      | analyst@empresa.com | analyst | Analyst User |
      | viewer@empresa.com  | viewer  | Viewer User  |
    Given I am on the login page                            # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:101
    When I enter invalid credentiInvalid email or password                        # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:196
    Then I see an error message "Invalid email or password" # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:202
    And I remain on the login page                          # None

  Scenario: User session expires                              # specs/features/authentication.feature:26
    Given the Supabase authentication is configured           # specs/steps/system_steps.py:37
    And the following users exist                             # specs/steps/system_steps.py:52
      | email               | role    | full_name    |
      | admin@empresa.com   | admin   | Admin User   |
      | analyst@empresa.com | analyst | Analyst User |
      | viewer@empresa.com  | viewer  | Viewer User  |
    Given I am logged in                                      # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:134
    When my session expires after inactivity                  # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:206
    Then I am redirected tSession expired, please login again                    # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:210
    And I see a message "Session expired, please login again" # None

  Scenario: User profile loads after login          # specs/features/authentication.feature:32
    Given the Supabase authentication is configured # specs/steps/system_steps.py:37
    And the following usersanalyst@empresa.com                   # specs/steps/system_steps.py:58
      | email               | role    | full_name    |
      | admin@empresa.com   | admin   | Admin User   |
      | analyst@empresa.com | analyst | Analyst User |
      | viewer@empresa.com  | viewer  | Viewer User  |
    Given I am logged in as "analyst@empresa.com"   # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:140
    When I navigate to my profile                   # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:214
    Then I see my full name, email, and role        # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:218
    And I can update my profile information         # None

Feature: Companies Management # specs/features/companies.feature:1
  As an analyst or admin
  I want to manage company registry data
  So that monthly cost records can be associated with companies
  Background:   # specs/features/companies.feature:6

  @analyst @admin
  Scenario: Register a new company           # specs/features/companies.feature:11
    Given the API is running                 # specs/steps/company_steps.py:10
    And I am logged in                       # specs/steps/system_steps.py:52
    Given I am on the "New Company" page     # specs/steps/company_steps.py:14
    When I fill in the company form          # specs/steps/company_steps.py:105
      | field        | value              |
      | company_id   | EMP001             |
      | empresa      | Empresa Alpha      |
      | cnpj         | 98.765.432/0001-10 |
      | razao_social | Alpha Ltda         |
      | cliente      | João Silva         |
      | email_envio  | joao@alpha.com     |
    And I save the company                   # specs/steps/company_steps.py:254
    Then the company is created successfully # specs/steps/company_steps.py:259
    And the API returns status 201           # specs/steps/company_steps.py:264
    And I see the company in the list        # None

  @analyst @admin
  Scenario: Company requires mandatory fields           # specs/features/companies.feature:27
    Given the API is running                            # specs/steps/company_steps.py:10
    And I am logged in                                  # specs/steps/system_steps.py:52
    Given I am on the "New Company" page                # specs/steps/company_steps.py:14
    When I leave "empresa" empty                        # specs/steps/company_steps.py:91
    And I save the company                              # specs/steps/company_steps.py:105
    Then I see a validation error "Empresa is required" # specs/steps/company_steps.py:273
    And the company is not created                      # specs/steps/company_steps.py:284

  @analyst @admin
  Scenario: Company CNPJ must be unique                                 # specs/features/companies.feature:35
    Given the API is running                                            # specs/steps/company_steps.py:10
    And I am logged in                                                  # specs/steps/system_steps.py:52
    Given a company exists with CNPJ "12.345.678/0001-90"               # specs/steps/company_steps.py:63
    When I try to create another company with CNPJ "12.345.678/0001-90" # specs/steps/company_steps.py:96
    And I save the company                                              # specs/steps/company_steps.py:105
    Then I see a validation error "CNPJ já cadastrado"                  # specs/steps/company_steps.py:273
    And the company is not created                                      # specs/steps/company_steps.py:284

  @analyst @admin @viewer
  Scenario: View companies list                                # specs/features/companies.feature:43
    Given the API is running                                   # specs/steps/company_steps.py:10
    And I am logged in                                         # specs/steps/system_steps.py:52
    Given companies exist in the system                        # specs/steps/company_steps.py:22
    When I navigate to "Companies" page                        # specs/steps/company_steps.py:247
    Then I see a list of all active companies                  # specs/steps/company_steps.py:289
    And each company shows: company_id, empresa, cnpj, cliente # specs/steps/company_steps.py:293

  @analyst @admin @viewer
  Scenario: View company details                                            # specs/features/companies.feature:50
    Given the API is running                                                # specs/steps/company_steps.py:10
    And I am logged in                                                      # specs/steps/system_steps.py:52
    Given a company exists with company_id "EMP001"                         # specs/steps/company_steps.py:30
    When I click on the company                                             # specs/steps/company_steps.py:221
    Then I see the full company details                                     # specs/steps/company_steps.py:300
    And I see all fields: empresa, cnpj, razao_social, cliente, email_envio # specs/steps/company_steps.py:305

  @analyst @admin
  Scenario: Update company information              # specs/features/companies.feature:57
    Given the API is running                        # specs/steps/company_steps.py:10
    And I am logged in                              # specs/steps/system_steps.py:52
    Given a company exists with company_id "EMP001" # specs/steps/company_steps.py:30
    And I am on the company detail page             # specs/steps/company_steps.py:18
    When I click "Edit Company"                     # specs/steps/company_steps.py:144
    And I change the cliente to "Maria Santos"      # specs/steps/company_steps.py:148
    And I click "Update"                            # specs/steps/company_steps.py:152
    Then the company is updated                     # specs/steps/company_steps.py:311
    And the cliente shows "Maria Santos"            # specs/steps/company_steps.py:316

  @analyst @admin
  Scenario: Deactivate a company                          # specs/features/companies.feature:67
    Given the API is running                              # specs/steps/company_steps.py:10
    And I am logged in                                    # specs/steps/system_steps.py:52
    Given a company exists with company_id "EMP001"       # specs/steps/company_steps.py:30
    When I click "Deactivate Company"                     # specs/steps/company_steps.py:173
    And I confirm company deactivation                    # specs/steps/company_steps.py:177
    Then the company is marked as inactive                # specs/steps/company_steps.py:322
    And it no longer appears in the active companies list # specs/steps/company_steps.py:328
    But its monthly records are preserved                 # specs/steps/company_steps.py:339

  @admin
  Scenario: Delete a company                          # specs/features/companies.feature:76
    Given the API is running                          # specs/steps/company_steps.py:10
    And I am logged in                                # specs/steps/system_steps.py:52
    Given a company exists with company_id "EMP003"   # specs/steps/company_steps.py:30
    When I click "Delete Company"                     # specs/steps/company_steps.py:197
    And I confirm company deletion                    # specs/steps/company_steps.py:201
    Then the company is permanently removed           # specs/steps/company_steps.py:345
    And all its monthly records are deleted (CASCADE) # specs/steps/system_steps.py:428

  @viewer
  Scenario: Viewer cannot create companies         # specs/features/companies.feature:84
    Given the API is running                       # specs/steps/company_steps.py:10
    And I am logged in                             # specs/steps/system_steps.py:52
    Given I am logged in as "viewer"               # specs/steps/system_steps.py:58
    When I navigate to the companies page          # specs/steps/company_steps.py:240
    Then I do not see a "New Company" button       # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:57
    And I cannot access the creation page directly # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:226

  @viewer
  Scenario: Viewer cannot edit companies       # specs/features/companies.feature:91
    Given the API is running                   # specs/steps/company_steps.py:10
    And I am logged in                         # specs/steps/system_steps.py:52
    Given a company exists                     # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:28
    And I am logged in as "viewer"             # specs/steps/system_steps.py:58
    When I view the company details            # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:42
    Then I do not see an "Edit" button         # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:230
    And I cannot access the edit page directly # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:234

  @viewer
  Scenario: Viewer cannot delete companies  # specs/features/companies.feature:99
    Given the API is running                # specs/steps/company_steps.py:10
    And I am logged in                      # specs/steps/system_steps.py:52
    Given a company exists                  # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:28
    And I am logged in as "viewer"          # specs/steps/system_steps.py:58
    When I view the company details         # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:42
    Then I do not see a "Delete" button     # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:61

Feature: Cost Centers Management # specs/features/cost_centers.feature:1
  As an analyst or admin
  I want to manage cost centers
  So that operational costs can be categorized
  Background:   # specs/features/cost_centers.feature:6

  @analyst @admin
  Scenario: Create cost center                   # specs/features/cost_centers.feature:10
    Given I am logged in                         # specs/steps/system_steps.py:52
    Given I am on the "New Cost Center" page     # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:69
    When I fill in the cost center form          # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:85
      | code        | INF                      |
      | name        | Infrastructure           |
      | description | Server and hosting costs |
    And I click "Save"                           # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:144
    Then the cost center is created successfully # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:149
    And I see the cost center in the list        # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:155
    And the cost center is active                # None

  @analyst @admin @viewer
  Scenario: View cost centers list                      # specs/features/cost_centers.feature:22
    Given I am logged in                                # specs/steps/system_steps.py:52
    Given cost centers exist in the system              # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:21
    When I navigate to "Cost Centers" page              # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:77
    Then I see a list of all active cost centers        # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:160
    And each cost center shows: code, name, description # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:164

  @analyst @admin
  Scenario: Update cost center                          # specs/features/cost_centers.feature:29
    Given I am logged in                                # specs/steps/system_steps.py:52
    Given a cost center exists with code "INF"          # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:65
    And I am on the cost center detail page             # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:73
    When I click "Edit"                                 # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:115
    And I change the name to "Infrastructure & Hosting" # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:119
    And I click "Save"                                  # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:85
    Then the cost center is updated                     # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:168
    And the name shows "Infrastructure & Hosting"       # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:173

  @admin
  Scenario: Deactivate cost center              # specs/features/cost_centers.feature:39
    Given I am logged in                        # specs/steps/system_steps.py:52
    Given a cost center exists with code "INF"  # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:65
    When I click "Deactivate"                   # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:123
    And I confirm the deactivation              # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:127
    Then the cost center is marked as inactive  # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:177
    And it no longer appears in the active list # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:182

  @viewer
  Scenario: Viewer cannot create cost centers      # specs/features/cost_centers.feature:47
    Given I am logged in                           # specs/steps/system_steps.py:52
    Given I am logged in as "viewer"               # specs/steps/system_steps.py:58
    When I navigate to the cost centers page       # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:17
    Then I do not see a "New Cost Center" button   # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:222
    And I cannot access the creation page directly # specs/steps/auth_steps.py:226

Feature: Monthly Cost Records # specs/features/monthly_records.feature:1
  As an analyst
  I want to enter monthly cost data per product
  So that the controller team can track expenses month by month
  Background:   # specs/features/monthly_records.feature:6

  @analyst @admin
  Scenario: Add monthly record for a product        # specs/features/monthly_records.feature:11
    Given the API is running                        # specs/steps/company_steps.py:10
    And I am logged in                              # specs/steps/system_steps.py:52
    Given company "EMP001" exists                   # specs/steps/monthly_steps.py:40
    When I add a monthly record                     # specs/steps/monthly_steps.py:291
      | field          | value      |
      | mes_ano        | 2026-01-01 |
      | elegiveis      | 100        |
      | vidas_cobradas | 95         |
      | valor_final    | 15000.00   |
    And I save the monthly record                   # specs/steps/monthly_steps.py:464
    Then the monthly record is created successfully # specs/steps/monthly_steps.py:470
    And the monthly API returns status 201          # None

  @analyst @admin
  Scenario: Duplicate month detection                                            # specs/features/monthly_records.feature:24
    Given the API is running                                                     # specs/steps/company_steps.py:10
    And I am logged in                                                           # specs/steps/system_steps.py:52
    Given company "EMP-DUP" exists                                               # specs/steps/monthly_steps.py:40
    And a monthly record for "EMP-DUP" + "2026-01-01"                            # specs/steps/monthly_steps.py:72
    When I try to add another record for the same company + month                # specs/steps/monthly_steps.py:278
    And I save the monthly record                                                # specs/steps/monthly_steps.py:291
    Then I see a monthly validation error "Record already exists for this month" # specs/steps/monthly_steps.py:482

  @analyst @admin
  Scenario: Add multiple records for same company   # specs/features/monthly_records.feature:32
    Given the API is running                        # specs/steps/company_steps.py:10
    And I am logged in                              # specs/steps/system_steps.py:52
    Given company "EMP001" exists                   # specs/steps/monthly_steps.py:40
    When I add a monthly record                     # specs/steps/monthly_steps.py:291
      | field       | value      |
      | mes_ano     | 2026-02-01 |
      | valor_final | 15000.00   |
    And I save the monthly record                   # specs/steps/monthly_steps.py:464
    Then the monthly record is created successfully # None

  @analyst @admin @viewer
  Scenario: View monthly records for a company           # specs/features/monthly_records.feature:42
    Given the API is running                             # specs/steps/company_steps.py:10
    And I am logged in                                   # specs/steps/system_steps.py:52
    Given company "EMP001" has monthly records           # specs/steps/monthly_steps.py:180
    When I retrieve monthly records for company "EMP001" # specs/steps/monthly_steps.py:354
    Then I see all monthly records for that company      # specs/steps/monthly_steps.py:500
    And each record shows: mes_ano, valor_final          # specs/steps/monthly_steps.py:506

  @analyst @admin @viewer
  Scenario: View records filtered by month                        # specs/features/monthly_records.feature:49
    Given the API is running                                      # specs/steps/company_steps.py:10
    And I am logged in                                            # specs/steps/system_steps.py:52
    Given monthly records exist for "2026-01-01" and "2026-02-01" # specs/steps/monthly_steps.py:196
    When I filter records by month "2026-01-01"                   # specs/steps/monthly_steps.py:378
    Then I see only records from January 2026                     # specs/steps/monthly_steps.py:514
    And I do not see February records                             # specs/steps/monthly_steps.py:521

  @analyst @admin @viewer
  Scenario: View all records across companies          # specs/features/monthly_records.feature:56
    Given the API is running                           # specs/steps/company_steps.py:10
    And I am logged in                                 # specs/steps/system_steps.py:52
    Given monthly records exist for multiple companies # specs/steps/monthly_steps.py:224
    When I retrieve all monthly records                # specs/steps/monthly_steps.py:390
    Then I see records from all companies              # specs/steps/monthly_steps.py:527
    And I can filter by company_id                     # specs/steps/monthly_steps.py:533

  @analyst @admin
  Scenario: Update a monthly record                           # specs/features/monthly_records.feature:63
    Given the API is running                                  # specs/steps/company_steps.py:10
    And I am logged in                                        # specs/steps/system_steps.py:52
    Given a monthly record exists for "EMP001" + "2026-01-01" # specs/steps/monthly_steps.py:111
    When I update the record                                  # specs/steps/monthly_steps.py:87
      | field       | value    |
      | valor_final | 16000.00 |
    And I save the update                                     # specs/steps/monthly_steps.py:476
    Then the monthly record is 16000.00                        # specs/steps/monthly_steps.py:492
    And the valor_final shows 16000.00                        # None

  @admin
  Scenario: Delete a monthly record                           # specs/features/monthly_records.feature:73
    Given the API is running                                  # specs/steps/company_steps.py:10
    And I am logged in                                        # specs/steps/system_steps.py:52
